{"id":"int-adf0ffd3671427164d0f72476bb114b7","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-08-09T08:45:13.011885Z","actor":"Justin Martin","issue_id":"syl-001.2.6","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Both halves landed and both run in CI. Verified rather than taken on report.\n\nTypeScript: shared/tests/fixtures.test.ts decodes the shipped fixtures, plus shared/tests/drift.test.ts as the generator gate. Run by npm test from the root in ci.yml.\n\nSwift: ios/SylKit/Tests/ContractTests/{ContractTests,FixtureLoader,SchemaRegistry}.swift. All 68 fixtures decode AND round-trip. Run by ios/scripts/test.sh in ios.yml.\n\nThe script runs BOTH swift test and xcodebuild test, with a comment in ios.yml explaining why: a scheme cannot run a local package's tests and xcodebuild reports success having run nothing. If CI ever runs only xcodebuild, the contract suite silently stops executing.\n\nThe gate earned itself on its first run — it caught a fifth Swift trap nobody predicted: ISO8601FormatStyle with fractional seconds explicitly enabled TRUNCATES milliseconds (.114Z decoded and re-encoded as .113Z), on every instant in every fixture. Invisible to decoding alone; only the round-trip sees it. That is exactly what a contract test is for."}}
